'''Demographic history''' is the reconstructed record of human population in the past. Given the lack of population records prior to the 1950s, there are many gaps in our record of demographic history. Historical demographers must make do with estimates, models and extrapolations. For the [[demographics|demographic]] methodology, see [[historical demography]].
